 the party he excites  people in the base and a lot of people  have been wondering for the last six  months where are you yeah and what do  you make of his decision to come out now  then I think Democrats see this as this  election as the future of democracy I  mean not not if we see unprecedent I've  said it several times right now but this  is something where I think they are  saying we need you we need somebody to  really tell tell the American people  what the stakes are the Senate  confirmation hearings for the Supreme  Court Brett Kavanaugh just wrapped what  was your takeaway  two things one Democrats didn't have a  knockout punch they certainly were able  to land a few punches but the stars of  these hearings were certainly the future  of the Democratic Party when you talk  about that Kamala Harris from California  Cory Booker from New Jersey really the  standouts for Democrats okay are they  trying to set themselves up essentially  for White House runs down the road is  that what that's about there's a lot of  speculation that this was them kind of  taking their moment and seizing on it  but I would say for a Democratic Party  that needs energy that you have all  these protesters that are there they  were really able to kind of be the new  face and what was their strategy I think  they were trying to find a way to kind  of punch them punch him and find ways to  kind of put some chinks in his armor  certainly they weren't able to find that  you know the The Smoking Gun that was  gonna take his Supreme Court nomination  we heard the news obviously about George  papadopolis there's also a report that  Paul Manafort may be weighing a plate  plea deal what can you tell us well the  one thing for sure  the circus is going to continue around  I've not started this this this case but  you know Paul Manafort has danced with  the idea for the past several weeks of  doing a potential plea deal if that  happens certainly everybody is watching  what he could flip the on